<section class="band"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="head rev"><div class="eyebrow">What we measure</div><h2>The business earns more, serves better and runs faster.</h2><p class="lead">Not a deck. These are the four things we measure.</p></div>
  <div class="rev"><div class="factors">
  <div><div class="fk">01 · MARGIN</div><h3>Less cost in delivery</h3><p>Replace manual process with software, without taking quality out with it.</p></div>
  <div><div class="fk">02 · THROUGHPUT</div><h3>More volume, same team</h3><p>Faster turnaround, shorter queues, fewer handoffs.</p></div>
  <div><div class="fk">03 · SERVICE</div><h3>A visibly better experience</h3><p>Because that is what renews contracts and wins referrals.</p></div>
  <div><div class="fk">04 · INSTITUTION</div><h3>Systems that outlast people</h3><p>Process, documentation and software that outlast any individual, including us.</p></div>
</div></div>
</div></section>
<section class="band"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="head rev"><div class="eyebrow">What we look for</div><h2>Narrow on purpose.</h2><p class="lead">A business that fits most of these is one where we can genuinely move the needle.</p></div>
  <div class="rev"><ul class="checklist"><li><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3.2 3L13 4.5"/></svg><span>A deep, defensible niche rather than a general-purpose service</span></li><li><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3.2 3L13 4.5"/></svg><span>Healthy gross margins with room to expand</span></li><li><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3.2 3L13 4.5"/></svg><span>Operations that are labour-intensive but genuinely replaceable with technology</span></li><li><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3.2 3L13 4.5"/></svg><span>Recurring or renewing revenue, ideally with developed-market customers</span></li><li><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3.2 3L13 4.5"/></svg><span>A regulatory, technological or geographic tailwind behind the sector</span></li><li><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M3 8.5l3.2 3L13 4.5"/></svg><span>An owner who wants the business to be better, not just bigger</span></li></ul></div>
</div></section>
<section class="band"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="head rev"><div class="eyebrow">How an engagement runs</div><h2>Four steps, in order.</h2></div>
  <div class="rev"><ol class="steps"><li><span class="n">01</span><h3>First conversation</h3><p>We look at the shape of the business, where the volume sits, and where the manual work concentrates. If we are not the right fit, we say so here rather than three months in.</p></li><li><span class="n">02</span><h3>Written scope</h3><p>What we are aiming at, what we will build, and the commercial terms, agreed in writing before anything begins.</p></li><li><span class="n">03</span><h3>Build and operate</h3><p>We work inside the operation, shipping in short cycles. You see something running early and use it well before it is finished.</p></li><li><span class="n">04</span><h3>Outcome</h3><p>Where the engagement is built toward one, the destination is a strategic event: a sale, a listing or a transition. Where it is not, the destination is simply a better business.</p></li></ol><div class="box" style="margin-top:40px"><p><b>Structure and terms.</b> Every engagement differs in depth and duration, so terms are set individually and documented before work starts. Indicative rates are on our <a class="inl" href="/pricing">pricing page</a>.</p><p>We work on select engagements. If you think there is a fit, you can connect with us at <a class="inl" href="mailto:adi@nevarrotech.com">adi@nevarrotech.com</a>.</p></div></div>
</div></section>
